    "body": "Consecutive facts ending in a known value such as Amber Field could store `now` as the owner instead of revising selvi's current record. The previous reader experiment amplified that stale state. This change adds an offline-learned writer-role correction that shares three nonpositive weights across candidate value primes while preserving the exact contextual boundary/direction and all parent model components. Actual generation now emits `selvi is in Amber Field.` with the complete version chain intact.\n\nRetain native artifact `231d6950`; the exact identity, local artifact, source hashes and raw receipts are bound in the evidence. Removing the extension restores parent `6f5ab4f3` byte-exactly. The native Rust path adds no serving matrix product, transformer, provider, phrase parser or vocabulary exception; this intervention fits no new H4 transforms.\n\nExecuted validation:\n\n- New construction 36/36 responses and complete revision chains; 1,057/1,057 inherited comparisons unchanged. Stress 16/16.\n- Frozen post-selection transfer 24/24: known-prime cases improve 3/12 to 12/12; unknown-value cases preserve 12/12. Familiar forms, with no refit.\n- All 14 earlier semantic/control reports and 12 multi-turn histories remain exact; retained word/Rust transfers and ordinary/stress Copy→Add/action panels pass.\n- 29 scoped native API checks and 17 focused tests pass, including actual allocation/checkpoint behavior at 218 input and 57 output positions. Generated Rust equalities and identifier-return fragments compile and execute. Formatting and claim wording checks pass.\n\nFour recent reverse-first-fact reader failures remain despite correct stored revisions. Full historical API, blanket suite, browser/WASM/HTTP and combined writer/current-source artifact are NOT_RUN. General prose/reasoning, alpha/frontier and complete-path energy remain unqualified. Both new removal switches perform the same ablation.\n\nCumulative model time is 28,853.580 / 31,350 seconds; this cycle used 1,053.360 model seconds. No time/storage extension, unique deletion or external paid compute. Preserve the prior reservation and 128 MiB storage margin. GitHub's five historical statuses are compatibility acknowledgements, not tests.\n\nReferences #973\n",
